taris-brcmfmac-dkms

The Broadcom FullMAC Wi-Fi driver (drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac, with the
headers of brcm80211/include) from Asahi Linux's kernel source, tag asahi-7.1.13-3
(https://github.com/AsahiLinux/linux), by Broadcom Corporation, its other authors and the Asahi
Linux contributors. Licensed under the ISC licence, as its files' SPDX lines say.

Changed by TarisOS (https://github.com/TarisOS/tarisOS) in 2026, in
0001-wifi-brcmfmac-pcie-BCM4378-L1-substates-only-while-the-firmware-runs.patch: the BCM4378's
PCIe link uses ASPM L1.1 and L1.2 while its firmware runs, and they're switched off before every
chip reset, so the firmware always starts with L1 alone, as at boot. pcie.c, the file it changes,
says so near its top (taris-notices.patch). Both patches are in TarisOS's source,
packaging/pkgbuilds/taris-brcmfmac-dkms.
